WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/feedback/QueryError.tsx — an inline error banner for a failed API query. It reduces the
    raw query `error` to the two bits it branches on (`status = isApiError(error) ? error.status : undefined`
    and `isTransientWaiting(error)`) and renders, through the shared `_ErrorState` chrome (a rose-tinted,
    backdrop-blurred, bordered tile: icon box + title + message + optional trailing CTA, with role/aria-live),
    one of five mutually-exclusive branches in this precedence:
      1. transient waiting (RateLimitError / UpstreamUnavailableError) → Clock, role=status/polite, NO CTA
         (the global RateLimitBanner owns the countdown) — t('error.waiting.title'|'.message').
      2. 404 → FileQuestion, t('error.notFound.title','{{thing}} not found',{thing}) with
         thing = resourceName ?? t('error.notFound.thingDefault','Resource'); optional "Back to list" CTA
         → navigate(listHref) only when listHref is supplied; t('error.notFound.message').
      3. 401 / 403 → Lock, t('error.unauthorized.title'|'.message'); "Sign in" CTA → '/login'.
      4. 5xx → Server, t('error.serverError.title'|'.message'); "Retry" CTA → onRetry (only when wired).
      5. network / unknown → isOffline = !online || status===0. Offline: WifiOff, role=status/polite,
         "Retry when online" CTA disabled, + a one-shot auto-retry on the window 'online' event (armed ONLY
         when error present && offline && onRetry wired && status===undefined). Online: AlertCircle,
         role=alert/assertive, "Retry" CTA → onRetry. t('error.network.*').
    `!error` → the component returns null.
  Documented data sources (prompt): useTranslation, useNavigate, useOnlineStatus.

SCOPE / ARCHITECTURE NOTE  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  An ATOMIC query-error primitive already exists: Sources/Components/Feedback/States.swift `TSQueryError` /
  `TSErrorDisplay` ("Query failure state with retry (web QueryError)"). That atomic component is OUT OF SCOPE
  here (prompt "Out of Scope: Atomic shared components"). This 0133 SHARED SURFACE is the higher-level,
  DATA-BOUND, multi-state QueryError HOST — it binds the failed-query error + online state (P1/S8), renders
  every state, resolves chrome via the P1/S10 facade, uses the P1/S9 tokens, navigates via the P1/S8 navigator
  seam (web useNavigate), and emits the P1/S11 view.opened telemetry. It reproduces the web `_ErrorState`
  composition as scoped subviews (rose-tinted icon box + title + message; facade-resolved strings via
  Text(verbatim:)) rather than calling TSErrorDisplay, for two parity reasons: (a) the web `_ErrorState` tints
  the WHOLE tile — icon box, title AND message — with the rose danger colour, where TSErrorDisplay uses neutral
  title/secondary text; and (b) the P1/S10 facade resolves to String, incompatible with TSErrorDisplay's
  LocalizedStringKey API. Same established precedent as the AlertBanner (0113) peer reproducing the web
  feedback body as scoped subviews. The full web QueryError contract (the five branches + the four CTAs + the
  offline auto-retry) is modelled by QueryFailure + QueryErrorMode.classify(failure:online:) +
  QueryErrorContent.make(...); the connectivity axis (web useOnlineStatus + the P4 stale freshness window) is
  the QueryErrorConnection axis with the leaf freshness chip.

